      <description><![CDATA[
        As Washington clamps down on military cooperation and slaps punitive tariffs on Ottawa, Canada is pivoting outward—injecting CAD 100 million into the NATO Innovation Fund to secure its defense tech future.
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ The announcement coincided with reports of a secret Pentagon memo restricting certain levels of US-Canada military cooperation.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Bilateral trade tensions have intensified, marked by 50-percent US tariffs on select Canadian goods and ongoing disputes over border enforcement.
